c meeting topic/time to decide what matters.\n4. Topic workflow:\n   - Use meeting title/description/agenda/linked docs to identify topic.\n   - Retrieve related Meeting_Notes, Slack, Drive docs if clearly relevant.\n   - Prefer current, topic-specific context over generic stale person history.\n5. Judgment pass:\n   - What does DJ need to know right before walking in?\n   - What changed since the last relevant meeting?\n   - What did DJ or others commit to, and is it done?\n   - What should DJ ask/decide/push/avoid?\n   - If evidence is weak, what opening question should DJ use to orient fast?\n\nOutput format per meeting:\n## [HH:MM AM/PM ET] [Meeting title]\n\n**Bottom line:** [one sentence: why this meeting matters now + how DJ should approach it]\n\n**Know walking in**\n- [specific current fact/context]\n- [specific prior follow-up/commitment/status]\n- [specific person/topic context]\n\n**DJ should**\n- [action/question/decision/posture]\n- [optional second/third; max 3]\n\n**Ask**\n\u201c[one sharp question]\u201d\n\nRules:\n- If no real DJ action, do not manufacture one; say what to listen for instead.\n- Do not include raw source dumps, progress receipts, or implementation notes.\n- If multiple qualifying meetings are due in the same run, produce one card per meeting, separated by a blank line.\n- If a calendar item is a travel block, personal block, focus block, or obvious non-meeting, output nothing for it.\n- If no qualifying real meeting is found, output exactly nothing.\n- Never schedule additional cron jobs from this job.",
